# Multi-group X11 keymap character injection fixes (apply to SELKIES_COMMIT
# 5686f6c4d20ed63a27e253bac00fb89ef99828c8; re-derive when bumping the pin).
#
# A session offering more than one GNOME input source (e.g. Swedish + US)
# gets a live XKB keymap with multiple *groups* on the same physical keys.
# input_handler.py's three keysym-injection paths (the printable-non-alpha
# branch of send_x11_keypress, the co,end handler, and the pynput branch for
# alphabetic characters including å/ä/ö) all delegated to xdotool/pynput's own
# keycode/modifier resolution, which has no concept of which group is
# currently active and no reliable way to target it. Symptoms: plain
# punctuation and å/ä/ö intermittently rendering as the wrong character,
# self-correcting on rapid repeat (":" -> "Ö", ">" -> ":", "<" -> "Z" or "|"
# depending on which input source was active) — plus, independently, AltGr-
# level characters ("|", "^") rendering as unrelated symbols ("×", "√") even
# with exactly the right modifier state genuinely held.
#
# All three call sites now route through two shared helpers instead:
#
# _whistler_resolve_keycode(keysym) — finds (keycode, level 0-3) via a LIVE
# get_keyboard_mapping() query (NOT self.xdisplay's cached
# keycode_to_keysym/keysym_to_keycode — that cache does not track GNOME's
# live keymap reconciliation, confirmed directly: a fresh connection found
# colon at keycode 60/level 1 while the cached one only found a level-3
# binding elsewhere, reproducing ":" -> "Ö" through supposedly-fixed code).
# Strictly prefers a match at index<4 (group 0, the group-independent quad)
# over index>=4 (a later XKB group, flattened into the same wide per-keycode
# list by this server — index%4 is only a valid "level" within group 0;
# treating a group-1 index the same way is what sent ">" through the
# physical Z key instead of the dedicated one).
#
# _whistler_xtest_inject(keysym, down) — for level 0/1 (no AltGr needed),
# injects directly via Xlib.ext.xtest.fake_input, explicitly synthesizing
# Shift only if the target level needs it and it isn't already genuinely
# held (checked against self.active_modifiers, not xdotool's own
# bookkeeping — xdotool's --clearmodifiers cleanup reproducibly left AltGr
# stuck held after a single ">", corrupting the next keystroke). Tracks
# exactly what each keydown synthesized so the matching keyup releases
# precisely that.
#
# For level>=2 (AltGr-involving) keysyms, delegates to
# _whistler_remap_inject(keysym, down) instead of trying to synthesize
# Shift+AltGr: GetKeyboardMapping's flat index does not reliably mean
# "index 2 = AltGr, index 3 = Shift+AltGr" (confirmed live — a receiver
# window showed exactly-correct Shift+AltGr state on the injected event,
# genuinely held per XQueryKeymap, and GNOME still delivered the wrong
# character). That mapping is actually governed by each key's XKB "type"
# definition, invisible through the core-protocol GetKeyboardMapping call —
# there is no reliable way to reverse-engineer it from there. Instead,
# _whistler_remap_inject sidesteps the ambiguity entirely: temporarily remap
# an unused ("scratch") keycode directly to the target keysym via
# XChangeKeyboardMapping, press that keycode bare with no modifiers at all
# (only "index 0" is ever read, unambiguous under every XKB type), then
# restore it to NoSymbol on release. Scoped to level>=2 only — level 0/1 was
# already reliable, and remapping broadcasts an X MappingNotify to every
# client on the display (each recomputes its keymap cache), worth avoiding
# for the common case.
#
# WHISTLER-DEBUG instrumentation throughout (grep that string) is kept at
# DEBUG level, not INFO — proven valuable multiple times during this
# investigation to correlate which of the three injection paths a given
# keystroke took, but too noisy for default INFO-level logs since it fires
# on every keystroke through these paths.
#
# Verified against a live session with an actual Mac keyboard driving both
# `sv` and `en` GNOME input sources: `:`, `<`, `>`, å/ä/ö, `|`, `^` all
# confirmed correct; XQueryKeymap confirmed no modifiers left stuck
# afterward. Full investigation narrative: design/keyboards.md.
--- a/src/selkies/input_handler.py
+++ b/src/selkies/input_handler.py
@@ -1249,6 +1249,178 @@
